title: Authorizations › Approved › Open an approved authorization
route: /authorizations?view=approved → /authorizations/case/ID
intro: The ways out of a ledger row (an approved authorization, or a request sent today that the ledger now tracks): the ID opens the full case, the row or its icon opens the tracked quick view, and the button does the one thing due. A case that is a request gets the Authorizations case page; one that only the ledger has gets the ledger case page; a case at a site the viewer is not looking at gets the out-of-site card.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: 26 of the 32 approved authorizations at the start have no request of their own and open the ledger case page; the other 6 are also requests, so they open the Authorizations case page. 'Start reauthorization' shows only for an approval ending within 7 days with no review open or booked. Every approved row at the start has a review this week, and signing books the next one, so it appears for a request sent today and approved, once Fast-forward brings its end within 7 days.
---
start s1 "A ledger row on screen (Approved, or With the payer marked 'New today')"
click c1 "Click the case ID (underlined)"
click c2 "Click the row away from a link or button, or its quick view icon"
goto gq "Continues in: Authorizations › Approved › Quick view of a tracked authorization"
click c3 "Click the row's button"

decision db "Which button does the row have?"
process b1 "A review not signed yet: the review's own button\n'Update the review', 'Review and sign', 'Check the review' or 'Open the review'"
store b1s "?review= and the review ID in the address"
goto gr "Continues in: Authorizations › Reviews this week › The review drawer"
process b2 "A denial waiting on a peer-to-peer call: 'Open the denial'"
goto gd "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › A denial opened"
process b3 "Approval ending within 7 days, no review open: 'Start reauthorization'"
process b3p "Go to New Case with type=reauth and the patient's case"
goto gn "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Intake › Reauthorization / renewal"
process b4 "Anything else: an outlined 'Open'"

process p1 "Go to /authorizations/case/ and the case ID"
decision ds "Is the case at a site the viewer is looking at?"
screen sos "Out-of-site card\n'This case is not available at Site A'\nNo patient or detail"
goto gs "Continues in: Authorizations › Sites › Reviews, step-down plans and ledger cases at each site"
decision d2 "Is the case a request: a queue record or a Dashboard request?"
screen s2 "Authorizations case page"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Ways in"
decision d3 "Is the case in the ledger?"
screen s3 "Ledger case page\nCase summary, next step, history\n'Open the review' (when one is due) and 'Back to Authorizations'"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › Ledger case page › Open and read"
screen s5 "'Request not found'\n(only for an address typed by hand)"
click c5 "Press the browser Back button"
process p5 "Authorizations again, on the same view and filters (they are in the address)\nSort and page start again"
end e1 "Back on the list"

s1 --> c1 --> p1
s1 --> c2 --> gq
s1 --> c3 --> db
db -->|Review open| b1 --> b1s --> gr
db -->|Peer-to-peer| b2 --> gd
db -->|Ending soon| b3 --> b3p --> gn
db -->|Other| b4 --> p1
p1 --> ds
ds -->|No| sos --> gs
ds -->|Yes| d2
d2 -->|Yes| s2 --> g1
d2 -->|No| d3
d3 -->|Yes| s3 --> g3
d3 -.->|No| s5
s2 --> c5
s3 --> c5
c5 --> p5 --> e1
